On Wednesday, June 04, 2014 11:50:51 Adam Lopresto wrote:
> Then {ri'u} becomes "Spatial tense. It indicates that the event is located
> to the right of a certain point when viewed from the origin. When tagging a
> sumti, the sumti specifies the point the event to the right of." with the
> same note.

In English, the use of "right" is inconsistent. Let's say I'm facing north, 
and north of me is Laura, who is facing south. In front of Laura is south of 
Laura. To the right of Laura is west of Laura.

Now suppose I'm facing north, and north of me is a house, whose front door is 
on the south side. In front of the house is south of the house. But to the 
right of the house is east of the house, or at least it was when I was drawing 
surveys of houses.

Now suppose I'm facing north, and north of me is a round column, which has no 
obvious front or left. Which way is right of the column? Which way is in front 
of the column?

How do these work in Lojban?

